    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0770" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51 Chase National Bank/7</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chase National
                    Bank</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-06-20"><hi rendition="#italic">June 20,
                        1928</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: With reference to letters of Messrs.
                    Rushmore, Bisbee and Stern<anchor n="22" xml:id="d674-f1"/> addressed to the
                    Department under dates of May 22 and June 14, 1928,<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d674-f2"/> regarding your interest in negotiating a credit
                    arrangement with the Cuban Government, I beg to inform you that, in the light of
                    the information at hand, the Department desires to offer <pb facs="0771" n="653"
                        xml:id="pg653"/> no objection to this proposed financing on the terms and
                    conditions set forth in the Supplemental Agreement enclosed with the
                    above-mentioned letter of June 14.</p>
                <p>You of course appreciate that, as pointed out in the Department’s announcement of
                    March 3, 1922,<anchor n="24" xml:id="d674-f3"/> the Department of State does not
                    pass upon the merits of foreign loans as business propositions nor assume any
                    responsibility in connection with such transactions, also that no reference to
                    the attitude of this Government should be made in any prospectus or
                    otherwise.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis
                            White</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                    Secretary</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
